From bc2eab1437066bc3cf19849b067c0c5dfa594d46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 14:09:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] mt-ui-tenant-picker: Redux tenant slice + RTK Query
 header injection + sidebar picker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Front-end half of the multi-tenant header story. The store keeps the
selected tenant id in a Redux slice, the RTK Query baseApi stamps
x-f5xc-tenant on every outbound request from that slice, and a sidebar
picker exposes the switch so a user can flip tenants without page
reloads.

Redux store
* slices/tenantSlice.ts (new) — selected tenant id + display label;
  setCurrentTenant / clearTenant reducers. localStorage hydration with
  try/catch fallback so a quota/disabled-storage error degrades to
  no-tenant rather than crashing the app on boot.
* apis/tenantsApi.ts (new) — RTK Query endpoints against
  /api/platform/tenants for list + get + create + update + delete.
* apis/baseApi.ts — prepareHeaders reads currentTenantID from state
  and adds x-f5xc-tenant. Single header-injection point; no per-
  endpoint changes needed. Adds "Tenants" tag for cache invalidation.
* apis/index.ts + slices/index.ts + store.ts — re-export + reducer
  wiring so the app picks up the new slice + api.
* hooks/useCurrentTenant.ts (new) — small reader hook with a setter
  that pushes through the slice so components don't import dispatch.

Components
* components/tenantBadge.tsx (new) — sidebar picker + inline "+ new
  tenant" form. Reads the tenants list from RTK Query, lets the user
  switch, shows the current identity. When only the seeded `default`
  tenant exists, the picker still renders for visual consistency.
* components/sidebar.tsx — mounts TenantBadge between SidebarHeader
  and the search box; hidden in the collapsed (icon-only) state.
  Branding swap (shaunfrost icons) intentionally NOT included — that's
  a fork-vanity change with no multi-tenant value.

Scope note: The `allow_private_network: true` default flip from
mt-header is NOT included. The NetworkConfig type at this patch base
doesn't carry the field, so the default doesn't exist yet — adding it
would also require schema/Go-side changes that are out of multi-tenant
scope. The operator can still flip allow_private_network per provider
via the existing provider edit form when the field lands upstream.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
